values
  ($m0$tq-aiml-what-is-ai-1$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-what-is-ai$m0$, $m0$What is the primary goal of Artificial Intelligence?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) To replace all human jobs immediately$m0$, $m0$B) To build systems that can perform tasks requiring human-like intelligence$m0$, $m0$C) To only perform basic arithmetic$m0$, $m0$D) To store large amounts of data without processing it$m0$), 1, $m0$AI focuses on creating systems capable of performing tasks — like perception, reasoning, and decision-making — that typically require human intelligence.$m0$, 1, 0),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-what-is-ai-2$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-what-is-ai$m0$, $m0$Which type of AI exists in practical use today?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) General AI$m0$, $m0$B) Super AI$m0$, $m0$C) Narrow AI$m0$, $m0$D) Self-Aware AI$m0$), 2, $m0$All AI systems currently in use — including voice assistants and recommendation engines — are examples of Narrow AI, designed for specific tasks.$m0$, 1, 1),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-what-is-ai-3$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-what-is-ai$m0$, $m0$What is the key difference between traditional programming and AI-based systems?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Traditional programs use explicit rules; AI systems often learn patterns from data$m0$, $m0$B) There is no real difference between them$m0$, $m0$C) AI systems cannot process any data$m0$, $m0$D) Traditional programs always run faster$m0$), 0, $m0$Traditional programming relies on manually written rules, while many AI systems (especially ML-based ones) learn patterns directly from data instead.$m0$, 1, 2),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-what-is-ai-4$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-what-is-ai$m0$, $m0$Which of these best describes "General AI"?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) AI that exists widely today in smartphones$m0$, $m0$B) A hypothetical AI with human-level intelligence across any task$m0$, $m0$C) A type of database software$m0$, $m0$D) A synonym for Narrow AI$m0$), 1, $m0$General AI refers to a still-hypothetical form of AI capable of performing any intellectual task a human can, which has not yet been achieved.$m0$, 1, 3),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-what-is-ai-5$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-what-is-ai$m0$, $m0$Which functionality-based AI type uses recent past data to inform its decisions?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Reactive Machines$m0$, $m0$B) Limited Memory$m0$, $m0$C) Theory of Mind$m0$, $m0$D) Self-Aware$m0$), 1, $m0$Limited Memory AI systems use recently observed data (like a self-driving car tracking nearby vehicle movements) to make more informed decisions.$m0$, 1, 4),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-what-is-ai-6$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-what-is-ai$m0$, $m0$Which of the following is a real-world example of Narrow AI?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) A fully conscious robot with human emotions$m0$, $m0$B) A spam email filter$m0$, $m0$C) A general-purpose AI that can do literally any human task$m0$, $m0$D) A theoretical machine with self-awareness$m0$), 1, $m0$A spam filter is designed for one specific task (detecting spam), making it a clear example of Narrow AI.$m0$, 1, 5),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-what-is-ai-7$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-what-is-ai$m0$, $m0$What is a common misconception about today's AI systems?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) That they can perform some helpful tasks$m0$, $m0$B) That they genuinely "understand" and "think" like humans do$m0$, $m0$C) That they are used in voice assistants$m0$, $m0$D) That they require data to function$m0$), 1, $m0$Most current AI systems recognize statistical patterns in data rather than genuinely understanding meaning the way humans do — this is a frequent point of confusion.$m0$, 1, 6),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-what-is-ai-8$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-what-is-ai$m0$, $m0$Which AI type, by functionality, is purely theoretical and involves machine consciousness?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Reactive Machines$m0$, $m0$B) Limited Memory$m0$, $m0$C) Self-Aware$m0$, $m0$D) Narrow AI$m0$), 2, $m0$Self-Aware AI is a speculative, far-future concept involving machine consciousness, which does not exist in any real system today.$m0$, 1, 7),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-what-is-ai-9$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-what-is-ai$m0$, $m0$Why might an AI system inherit biases?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) AI systems cannot be biased under any circumstances$m0$, $m0$B) Because they learn patterns from data, which may itself contain biases$m0$, $m0$C) Because all AI systems are programmed with explicit bias rules$m0$, $m0$D) Bias only affects traditional programs, never AI$m0$), 1, $m0$Since many AI systems learn directly from data, any biases present in that training data can be reflected or amplified in the system's behavior.$m0$, 1, 8),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-what-is-ai-10$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-what-is-ai$m0$, $m0$Which of these is NOT one of the three capability-based types of AI discussed?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Narrow AI$m0$, $m0$B) General AI$m0$, $m0$C) Super AI$m0$, $m0$D) Reactive AI$m0$), 3, $m0$"Reactive" is a functionality-based classification (Reactive Machines), not one of the three capability-based types (Narrow, General, Super AI).$m0$, 1, 9)
