  ($m0$tq-aiml-data-cleaning-9$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-data-cleaning$m0$, $m0$Why is "garbage in, garbage out" relevant to data cleaning?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) It means ML models can fix any data quality issue automatically$m0$, $m0$B) It means poor-quality input data leads to poor-quality results, regardless of the algorithm used$m0$, $m0$C) It only applies to image data$m0$, $m0$D) It has no relevance to Machine Learning$m0$), 1, $m0$This phrase emphasizes that no algorithm, however powerful, can produce reliable results from fundamentally flawed or messy input data.$m0$, 1, 8),
