values
  ($m0$tq-aiml-linear-regression-1$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-linear-regression$m0$, $m0$What does the "slope" (m) represent in Linear Regression?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) The value of y when x is zero$m0$, $m0$B) How much y changes for each unit increase in x$m0$, $m0$C) The total number of data points$m0$, $m0$D) The average of all y values$m0$), 1, $m0$The slope quantifies the rate of change in the output (y) for every one-unit increase in the input (x).$m0$, 1, 0),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-linear-regression-2$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-linear-regression$m0$, $m0$What does the "intercept" (b) represent?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) The slope of the line$m0$, $m0$B) The value of y when x equals 0$m0$, $m0$C) The total error of the model$m0$, $m0$D) The number of features used$m0$), 1, $m0$The intercept is the point where the line crosses the y-axis — the predicted value of y when x is 0.$m0$, 1, 1),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-linear-regression-3$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-linear-regression$m0$, $m0$Which cost function is most commonly used to fit a Linear Regression line?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Accuracy$m0$, $m0$B) Mean Squared Error (MSE)$m0$, $m0$C) Precision$m0$, $m0$D) Entropy$m0$), 1, $m0$MSE measures the average squared difference between actual and predicted values, and Linear Regression finds the line that minimizes it.$m0$, 1, 2),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-linear-regression-4$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-linear-regression$m0$, $m0$Why is Linear Regression sensitive to outliers?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Outliers have no effect on the fitted line$m0$, $m0$B) Squaring errors in MSE gives extra weight to large deviations, which outliers often cause$m0$, $m0$C) Outliers are automatically removed by the algorithm$m0$, $m0$D) Linear Regression cannot process numeric data$m0$), 1, $m0$Since MSE squares each error, unusually large errors from outliers are weighted even more heavily, pulling the fitted line disproportionately toward them.$m0$, 1, 3),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-linear-regression-5$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-linear-regression$m0$, $m0$What does `model.coef_` return in Scikit-learn's LinearRegression?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) The predicted values$m0$, $m0$B) The learned slope(s) of the model$m0$, $m0$C) The dataset's mean$m0$, $m0$D) The number of training examples$m0$), 1, $m0$`coef_` stores the learned slope (or slopes, for multiple features) that the model determined during training.$m0$, 1, 4),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-linear-regression-6$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-linear-regression$m0$, $m0$Which of these relationships would Linear Regression model well?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) A relationship that curves sharply upward and downward$m0$, $m0$B) A relationship that is roughly a straight line$m0$, $m0$C) A relationship with no pattern at all$m0$, $m0$D) A relationship that only exists for categorical data$m0$), 1, $m0$Linear Regression is specifically designed to model relationships that can be reasonably approximated by a straight line.$m0$, 1, 5),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-linear-regression-7$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-linear-regression$m0$, $m0$What is the main limitation of Simple Linear Regression compared to Multiple Linear Regression?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) It cannot make any predictions$m0$, $m0$B) It only considers a single input feature$m0$, $m0$C) It always performs worse in every situation$m0$, $m0$D) It requires no training data$m0$), 1, $m0$Simple Linear Regression uses only one input feature, while Multiple Linear Regression can incorporate several features simultaneously.$m0$, 1, 6),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-linear-regression-8$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-linear-regression$m0$, $m0$If a Linear Regression model learns `y = 5x + 10`, what is the predicted value when x = 4?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) 14$m0$, $m0$B) 20$m0$, $m0$C) 30$m0$, $m0$D) 40$m0$), 2, $m0$y = 5(4) + 10 = 20 + 10 = 30.$m0$, 1, 7),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-linear-regression-9$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-linear-regression$m0$, $m0$Why is visualizing data with a scatter plot recommended before applying Linear Regression?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) It has no practical benefit$m0$, $m0$B) It helps confirm whether a linear relationship is actually a reasonable assumption$m0$, $m0$C) It automatically trains the model$m0$, $m0$D) It replaces the need for any evaluation metrics$m0$), 1, $m0$A scatter plot provides a quick visual check of whether the data's pattern is genuinely close to linear, before committing to this modeling approach.$m0$, 1, 8),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-linear-regression-10$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-linear-regression$m0$, $m0$Which of these is a real-world application of Linear Regression?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Grouping customers into segments with no known outcome$m0$, $m0$B) Predicting house prices based on size$m0$, $m0$C) Detecting the most frequent word in a document$m0$, $m0$D) Learning to play a game through trial and error$m0$), 1, $m0$Predicting a continuous numeric value (price) from a numeric feature (size) is a classic Linear Regression use case.$m0$, 1, 9)
