insert into public.test_questions (id, test_id, question_text, options, correct_index, explanation, marks, sort_order)
values
  ($m0$tq-aiml-random-forest-1$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-random-forest$m0$, $m0$What is the core idea behind Random Forest?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Building a single, very deep Decision Tree$m0$, $m0$B) Combining many Decision Trees to produce a more robust, accurate prediction$m0$, $m0$C) Using only one feature for every split$m0$, $m0$D) Replacing all Decision Trees with Linear Regression$m0$), 1, $m0$Random Forest is an ensemble method that combines the predictions of many individual Decision Trees to improve accuracy and stability.$m0$, 1, 0),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-random-forest-2$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-random-forest$m0$, $m0$What is "bootstrap sampling" in the context of Random Forest?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Training all trees on the exact same full dataset$m0$, $m0$B) Randomly sampling subsets of the training data (with replacement) for each individual tree$m0$, $m0$C) Removing all missing values from the dataset$m0$, $m0$D) Scaling all numeric features$m0$), 1, $m0$Bootstrap sampling creates a randomly selected subset of the training data (with replacement) for each tree, promoting diversity across the forest's individual trees.$m0$, 1, 1),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-random-forest-3$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-random-forest$m0$, $m0$How does Random Forest make a final classification prediction?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) By using only the very first tree's prediction$m0$, $m0$B) By majority vote across all individual trees' predictions$m0$, $m0$C) By always predicting the most common class in the entire dataset$m0$, $m0$D) By randomly selecting one tree's prediction$m0$), 1, $m0$Each tree in the forest "votes" for a class, and Random Forest predicts whichever class receives the most votes overall.$m0$, 1, 2),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-random-forest-4$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-random-forest$m0$, $m0$Why does Random Forest tend to overfit less than a single Decision Tree?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) It uses fewer training examples overall$m0$, $m0$B) Averaging across many diverse trees reduces the impact of any single tree's overfitting$m0$, $m0$C) It never uses more than one feature$m0$, $m0$D) It doesn't actually use Decision Trees internally$m0$), 1, $m0$Combining many trees, each with slightly different data and features, helps smooth out individual trees' tendency to overfit, since errors from different trees tend to cancel out.$m0$, 1, 3),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-random-forest-5$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-random-forest$m0$, $m0$What does the `n_estimators` parameter control in `RandomForestClassifier`?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) The maximum depth of each tree$m0$, $m0$B) The number of individual trees in the forest$m0$, $m0$C) The number of features in the dataset$m0$, $m0$D) The learning rate$m0$), 1, $m0$`n_estimators` specifies how many individual Decision Trees will be built and combined within the Random Forest.$m0$, 1, 4),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-random-forest-6$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-random-forest$m0$, $m0$What does `model.feature_importances_` provide?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) The raw training data$m0$, $m0$B) A score for each feature indicating its overall contribution to the model's predictions$m0$, $m0$C) The exact structure of every individual tree$m0$, $m0$D) The model's accuracy score$m0$), 1, $m0$Feature importances quantify how much each feature contributed, on average across all trees, to reducing impurity — offering a useful interpretability tool.$m0$, 1, 5),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-random-forest-7$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-random-forest$m0$, $m0$What is a key tradeoff when using Random Forest instead of a single Decision Tree?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Random Forest is always faster and simpler$m0$, $m0$B) Random Forest generally sacrifices some interpretability in exchange for improved accuracy and stability$m0$, $m0$C) Random Forest cannot be used for classification$m0$, $m0$D) There is no meaningful tradeoff at all$m0$), 1, $m0$While Random Forest typically performs better and more reliably, it's harder to interpret than tracing a single, simple Decision Tree's logic.$m0$, 1, 6),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-random-forest-8$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-random-forest$m0$, $m0$Which of these best describes "ensemble learning"?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Using only a single powerful model$m0$, $m0$B) Combining multiple models to produce a more robust overall prediction$m0$, $m0$C) A technique used exclusively for regression$m0$, $m0$D) A method for removing missing values$m0$), 1, $m0$Ensemble learning refers to combining the strengths of multiple models to achieve better overall performance than any single model alone.$m0$, 1, 7),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-random-forest-9$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-random-forest$m0$, $m0$Why does Random Forest randomly select a subset of features at each split, rather than considering all features?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) To save memory only, with no effect on predictions$m0$, $m0$B) To increase diversity among the individual trees, reducing correlation between their errors$m0$, $m0$C) Because using all features is not technically possible$m0$, $m0$D) To make each tree identical to the others$m0$), 1, $m0$Restricting each split to a random subset of features encourages the individual trees to differ from one another, which strengthens the overall ensemble when their predictions are combined.$m0$, 1, 8),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-random-forest-10$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-random-forest$m0$, $m0$Which Scikit-learn class implements Random Forest for classification tasks?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) `DecisionTreeClassifier`$m0$, $m0$B) `RandomForestClassifier`$m0$, $m0$C) `KNeighborsClassifier`$m0$, $m0$D) `LogisticRegression`$m0$), 1, $m0$`RandomForestClassifier` is the standard Scikit-learn implementation of the Random Forest algorithm for classification problems.$m0$, 1, 9)
on conflict (id) do nothing;

