  ($m0$tq-aiml-pca-principal-component-analysis-8$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-pca-principal-component-analysis$m0$, $m0$What is a key limitation of PCA regarding interpretability?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) PCA components are always more interpretable than original features$m0$, $m0$B) Principal components are mathematical combinations of original features, making them harder to directly interpret$m0$, $m0$C) PCA cannot be visualized in any way$m0$, $m0$D) PCA removes the need for any further analysis$m0$), 1, $m0$Since principal components are artificial constructs (weighted combinations of multiple original features), they lack the direct, intuitive meaning of the original features.$m0$, 1, 7),
