insert into public.test_questions (id, test_id, question_text, options, correct_index, explanation, marks, sort_order)
values
  ($m0$tq-aiml-feature-engineering-1$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-feature-engineering$m0$, $m0$What is the main goal of Feature Engineering?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) To remove irrelevant existing features$m0$, $m0$B) To create new, more informative features from existing raw data$m0$, $m0$C) To split data into training and test sets$m0$, $m0$D) To calculate summary statistics only$m0$), 1, $m0$Feature Engineering focuses on constructing new features that better expose useful patterns for the model to learn from.$m0$, 1, 0),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-feature-engineering-2$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-feature-engineering$m0$, $m0$What is an "interaction feature"?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) A feature created by removing another feature$m0$, $m0$B) A new feature formed by combining two existing features (e.g., multiplying them)$m0$, $m0$C) A feature extracted directly from a date column$m0$, $m0$D) A feature with only categorical values$m0$), 1, $m0$Interaction features capture the combined effect of two existing features, often by multiplying them together.$m0$, 1, 1),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-feature-engineering-3$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-feature-engineering$m0$, $m0$Why might polynomial features help a Linear Regression model?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) They remove the need for any training data$m0$, $m0$B) They allow the model to capture curved (non-linear) relationships while still using linear regression techniques$m0$, $m0$C) They always improve model accuracy regardless of the data$m0$, $m0$D) They convert continuous data into categories$m0$), 1, $m0$By adding transformed versions of a feature (like x²), a linear model can effectively fit curved relationships between that feature and the target.$m0$, 1, 2),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-feature-engineering-4$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-feature-engineering$m0$, $m0$Which of these is an example of extracting a feature from a date?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Multiplying two numeric columns together$m0$, $m0$B) Extracting the day-of-week or a weekend flag from a timestamp$m0$, $m0$C) Removing a column entirely$m0$, $m0$D) Scaling a numeric feature to a 0-1 range$m0$), 1, $m0$Date extraction pulls out useful components (like day-of-week) that aren't directly usable from the raw timestamp alone.$m0$, 1, 3),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-feature-engineering-5$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-feature-engineering$m0$, $m0$What does "binning" do to a continuous feature?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Converts it into a smaller set of discrete categories$m0$, $m0$B) Removes it from the dataset entirely$m0$, $m0$C) Converts it into a date format$m0$, $m0$D) Doubles its numeric value$m0$), 0, $m0$Binning groups continuous values into a smaller number of discrete categories or ranges (e.g., age groups).$m0$, 1, 4),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-feature-engineering-6$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-feature-engineering$m0$, $m0$How does Feature Engineering differ from Feature Selection (Module 3)?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) They are exactly the same technique$m0$, $m0$B) Feature Engineering creates new features; Feature Selection chooses among existing ones$m0$, $m0$C) Feature Selection always creates more features than Feature Engineering$m0$, $m0$D) Feature Engineering only applies to categorical data$m0$), 1, $m0$This is the fundamental distinction — Feature Engineering constructs new features, while Feature Selection narrows down which existing features to keep.$m0$, 1, 5),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-feature-engineering-7$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-feature-engineering$m0$, $m0$Which Scikit-learn class helps generate polynomial features automatically?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) `StandardScaler`$m0$, $m0$B) `PolynomialFeatures`$m0$, $m0$C) `LabelEncoder`$m0$, $m0$D) `SimpleImputer`$m0$), 1, $m0$`PolynomialFeatures` automatically generates polynomial and interaction terms from existing numeric features.$m0$, 1, 6),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-feature-engineering-8$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-feature-engineering$m0$, $m0$Why might creating too many high-degree polynomial features be risky?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) It always improves model performance with no downsides$m0$, $m0$B) It can increase overfitting risk, since the model becomes more complex$m0$, $m0$C) It automatically removes irrelevant features$m0$, $m0$D) It has no effect on model complexity$m0$), 1, $m0$Adding many high-degree polynomial features significantly increases model complexity, raising the risk of overfitting (Topic 1) if not carefully managed.$m0$, 1, 7),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-feature-engineering-9$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-feature-engineering$m0$, $m0$What must be ensured when applying feature engineering steps to a machine learning pipeline?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) They only need to be applied to the training set$m0$, $m0$B) The same transformations must be applied consistently to both training and test/new data$m0$, $m0$C) Feature engineering steps should differ between training and test sets$m0$, $m0$D) Feature engineering has no bearing on test data at all$m0$), 1, $m0$Just like scaling and encoding, feature engineering transformations must be applied identically to training and test data to ensure consistent, valid model behavior.$m0$, 1, 8),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-feature-engineering-10$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-feature-engineering$m0$, $m0$Why is domain knowledge particularly valuable for Feature Engineering?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Domain knowledge is irrelevant to this process$m0$, $m0$B) It helps identify which new features are likely to be genuinely meaningful and predictive for the specific problem$m0$, $m0$C) Domain knowledge only matters for Feature Selection, not Feature Engineering$m0$, $m0$D) Feature Engineering can be fully automated without any human input$m0$), 1, $m0$Understanding the real-world context of a problem helps guide which combinations, extractions, or transformations are likely to reveal genuinely useful patterns, rather than creating features blindly.$m0$, 1, 9)
on conflict (id) do nothing;

