values
  ($m0$tq-aiml-scikit-learn-1$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-scikit-learn$m0$, $m0$What is the consistent method used to train nearly any Scikit-learn model or preprocessor?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) `.train()`$m0$, $m0$B) `.fit()`$m0$, $m0$C) `.learn()`$m0$, $m0$D) `.build()`$m0$), 1, $m0$`.fit()` is the standard method across Scikit-learn used to train models and fit preprocessing transformations on data.$m0$, 1, 0),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-scikit-learn-2$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-scikit-learn$m0$, $m0$What does a Scikit-learn `Pipeline` do?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) It deletes unnecessary columns automatically$m0$, $m0$B) It chains preprocessing and modeling steps into a single object, applied consistently$m0$, $m0$C) It only works with classification algorithms$m0$, $m0$D) It replaces the need for a train-test split$m0$), 1, $m0$`Pipeline` bundles multiple steps together, ensuring they're applied in the correct order and preventing data leakage between training and test data.$m0$, 1, 1),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-scikit-learn-3$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-scikit-learn$m0$, $m0$Which Scikit-learn module contains `train_test_split` and `GridSearchCV`?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) `sklearn.preprocessing`$m0$, $m0$B) `sklearn.model_selection`$m0$, $m0$C) `sklearn.metrics`$m0$, $m0$D) `sklearn.linear_model`$m0$), 1, $m0$`sklearn.model_selection` contains tools for splitting data and tuning models, including `train_test_split`, `cross_val_score`, and `GridSearchCV`.$m0$, 1, 2),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-scikit-learn-4$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-scikit-learn$m0$, $m0$Which module would you use to find `accuracy_score` and `confusion_matrix`?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) `sklearn.metrics`$m0$, $m0$B) `sklearn.cluster`$m0$, $m0$C) `sklearn.datasets`$m0$, $m0$D) `sklearn.impute`$m0$), 0, $m0$`sklearn.metrics` houses the evaluation functions covered throughout Module 6, including `accuracy_score` and `confusion_matrix`.$m0$, 1, 3),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-scikit-learn-5$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-scikit-learn$m0$, $m0$Why does using a `Pipeline` help prevent data leakage?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) It has no effect on data leakage at all$m0$, $m0$B) It ensures preprocessing steps are fit only on training data, then correctly applied (not re-fit) to test data$m0$, $m0$C) It automatically deletes the test set$m0$, $m0$D) It only works with a single algorithm$m0$), 1, $m0$By fitting the entire pipeline once on training data, subsequent calls on test data correctly apply the already-fitted transformations, rather than accidentally re-fitting on test data.$m0$, 1, 4),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-scikit-learn-6$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-scikit-learn$m0$, $m0$Can Scikit-learn be used to build and train Deep Learning neural networks?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Yes, it is the primary library for Deep Learning$m0$, $m0$B) No, Scikit-learn focuses on traditional ML; Deep Learning requires frameworks like TensorFlow or PyTorch$m0$, $m0$C) Scikit-learn and TensorFlow are exactly the same library$m0$, $m0$D) Deep Learning doesn't require any specialized library$m0$), 1, $m0$Scikit-learn is designed for traditional ML algorithms; Deep Learning/neural network tasks require dedicated frameworks like TensorFlow or PyTorch, covered in Module 10.$m0$, 1, 5),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-scikit-learn-7$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-scikit-learn$m0$, $m0$What is `sklearn.datasets` primarily used for?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Storing a model's final predictions$m0$, $m0$B) Providing small built-in datasets and synthetic data generators for practice/testing$m0$, $m0$C) Performing feature scaling$m0$, $m0$D) Calculating evaluation metrics$m0$), 1, $m0$This module offers convenient, ready-to-use datasets (like `load_iris`) and generators (like `make_classification`), useful for quick experimentation.$m0$, 1, 6),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-scikit-learn-8$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-scikit-learn$m0$, $m0$Which module would contain `RandomForestClassifier`?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) `sklearn.ensemble`$m0$, $m0$B) `sklearn.linear_model`$m0$, $m0$C) `sklearn.preprocessing`$m0$, $m0$D) `sklearn.metrics`$m0$), 0, $m0$Ensemble methods like Random Forest, Bagging, and Boosting classifiers are housed in `sklearn.ensemble`.$m0$, 1, 7),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-scikit-learn-9$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-scikit-learn$m0$, $m0$What is a key advantage of Scikit-learn's consistent API design?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) It only works with one single algorithm$m0$, $m0$B) Once you learn the fit/predict/transform pattern, it applies similarly across dozens of different algorithms$m0$, $m0$C) It eliminates the need to understand any ML concepts$m0$, $m0$D) It requires a completely different syntax for every new algorithm$m0$), 1, $m0$This consistency is precisely why switching between, say, `LinearRegression` and `RandomForestClassifier` requires learning very little new syntax.$m0$, 1, 8),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-scikit-learn-10$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-scikit-learn$m0$, $m0$Which of these is a genuine limitation of Scikit-learn?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) It has poor documentation$m0$, $m0$B) It isn't designed for Deep Learning tasks or extremely large, out-of-memory datasets$m0$, $m0$C) It cannot perform any classification tasks$m0$, $m0$D) It requires a paid license$m0$), 1, $m0$Scikit-learn is built for traditional ML on data that fits in memory; Deep Learning and big-data-scale problems require other specialized tools.$m0$, 1, 9)
