insert into public.test_questions (id, test_id, question_text, options, correct_index, explanation, marks, sort_order)
values
  ($m0$tq-aiml-generative-ai-1$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-generative-ai$m0$, $m0$What is the key difference between generative and discriminative models?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) There is no real difference between them$m0$, $m0$B) Generative models create new content; discriminative models classify or predict from existing data$m0$, $m0$C) Discriminative models create new content; generative models only classify data$m0$, $m0$D) Both terms refer to exactly the same technique$m0$), 1, $m0$This is the fundamental distinction — generative models produce new, original content, while discriminative models (covered throughout Modules 4-7) analyze and classify existing data.$m0$, 1, 0),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-generative-ai-2$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-generative-ai$m0$, $m0$What are the two competing networks in a GAN?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) A scaler and an encoder$m0$, $m0$B) A Generator and a Discriminator$m0$, $m0$C) An optimizer and a loss function$m0$, $m0$D) A CNN and an RNN$m0$), 1, $m0$A GAN consists of a Generator (creating fake content) and a Discriminator (trying to distinguish fake from real), which improve together through their ongoing competition.$m0$, 1, 1),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-generative-ai-3$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-generative-ai$m0$, $m0$How does a Diffusion Model generate an image?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) By directly copying an existing training image$m0$, $m0$B) By starting from random noise and gradually "cleaning it up" into a coherent image$m0$, $m0$C) By using two competing networks, exactly like a GAN$m0$, $m0$D) It cannot generate images at all$m0$), 1, $m0$Diffusion models learn to reverse a noise-adding process, starting from pure noise and progressively refining it into a realistic image.$m0$, 1, 2),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-generative-ai-4$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-generative-ai$m0$, $m0$What is a known limitation of generative AI, especially for text generation?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) It is always perfectly factually accurate$m0$, $m0$B) It can produce plausible-sounding but factually incorrect content ("hallucination")$m0$, $m0$C) It cannot generate any text at all$m0$, $m0$D) It only works with numeric data$m0$), 1, $m0$Generative text models can produce fluent, convincing-sounding text that is nonetheless factually wrong — a well-known limitation explored further in Topic 8.$m0$, 1, 3),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-generative-ai-5$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-generative-ai$m0$, $m0$Which of these is an example of a discriminative task (not generative)?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Generating a new image from a text description$m0$, $m0$B) Classifying an email as spam or not spam$m0$, $m0$C) Writing an original poem$m0$, $m0$D) Creating new music$m0$), 1, $m0$Spam classification is a discriminative task — it analyzes existing input and assigns a category, rather than creating new content.$m0$, 1, 4),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-generative-ai-6$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-generative-ai$m0$, $m0$In a GAN, what happens as the Discriminator improves at catching fakes?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) The Generator stops improving entirely$m0$, $m0$B) The Generator is forced to improve as well, in order to keep producing convincing fakes$m0$, $m0$C) Both networks are deleted$m0$, $m0$D) The Discriminator becomes irrelevant$m0$), 1, $m0$GANs improve through this adversarial competition — as one network gets better, it pushes the other to improve as well.$m0$, 1, 5),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-generative-ai-7$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-generative-ai$m0$, $m0$Why might generative AI raise ethical or legal questions?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) It has no relationship to ethical or legal considerations$m0$, $m0$B) Concerns around copyright, misinformation (e.g., deepfakes), and the training data used are genuinely significant$m0$, $m0$C) Generative AI is entirely risk-free$m0$, $m0$D) These concerns only apply to discriminative models$m0$), 1, $m0$The ability to generate convincing new content raises real, actively-discussed concerns around copyright, misuse for misinformation, and the sourcing of training data.$m0$, 1, 6),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-generative-ai-8$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-generative-ai$m0$, $m0$What foundational architecture underlies most modern text-based generative AI (LLMs)?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Simple Linear Regression$m0$, $m0$B) The Transformer architecture (introduced in Topic 6)$m0$, $m0$C) K-Means clustering$m0$, $m0$D) Basic Decision Trees$m0$), 1, $m0$As introduced in Topic 6, the Transformer architecture is the foundation for virtually all modern text-generation systems, including LLMs (Topic 8).$m0$, 1, 7),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-generative-ai-9$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-generative-ai$m0$, $m0$Which statement correctly reflects a generative AI model's "understanding" of content?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) It reasons about content exactly the way a human does$m0$, $m0$B) It generates statistically plausible output based on learned patterns, which is different from genuine human-like comprehension$m0$, $m0$C) It has no relationship to patterns learned from training data$m0$, $m0$D) It always produces perfectly original, entirely unprecedented content with no relationship to training data$m0$), 1, $m0$Generative models produce output based on statistical patterns learned from data, which is a meaningfully different process from genuine human understanding or reasoning.$m0$, 1, 8),
  ($m0$tq-aiml-generative-ai-10$m0$, $m0$mt-aiml-generative-ai$m0$, $m0$Which of these is a genuine, practical application of Generative AI?$m0$, jsonb_build_array($m0$A) Detecting whether a transaction is fraudulent$m0$, $m0$B) Creating an original image from a text description$m0$, $m0$C) Predicting a house's sale price$m0$, $m0$D) Grouping customers into segments$m0$), 1, $m0$Generating new, original content (like an image from a text prompt) is a defining, practical application of Generative AI — the other options are all discriminative/analytical tasks.$m0$, 1, 9)
on conflict (id) do nothing;

